        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Done. The difference between the plasmids is a 39 bp insertion (part of BBa_I746360) after position 213 of the input, so a single primer pair suffices.\n\n**primers.fasta:**\n```\n>BBa_I746360_ins_F\nagcaagggcgaggagagtagattagaagaagaattaagaagaagattaacagaa\n>BBa_I746360_ins_R\ncatatgtatatctccttcttaaagttaaac\n```\n\nDetails:\n- **Forward primer:** 15 nt anneal to input (`agcaagggcgaggag`, Tm = 59.54 °C per oligotm with the specified flags) + the full 39 nt insertion as 5′ tail.\n- **Reverse primer:** 30 nt fully annealing to input upstream of the insertion site (Tm = 58.08 °C).\n- Both annealing regions are within 15–45 nt, Tms within 58–72 °C, and differ by only ~1.5 °C.\n- Verified in silico: PCR with linearized amplification and blunt re-ligation regenerates exactly the output plasmid sequence.",
            "session_id": "tb-1309d0abd7"
        }
